(a) The building and land use administrator shall have the following duties and responsibilities:
(1) To familiarize himself with all ordinances, codes, regulations, and procedures applicable in the city, pertaining to zoning, land use, subdivisions, building construction, fences, and related permits;
(2) To assist individuals, business entities and other organizations in the process of applying for permits for buildings, other structures (including fences), and land use within the city, providing them with pertinent information and guidance regarding the application and approval process and applicable ordinances, codes, regulations and procedures while also communicating that the municipal planning commission or other appropriate agency has the ultimate authority to grant or deny such permits;
(3) To receive and review applications and related plans and specifications for permits for the construction of buildings and other structures (including fences) and for other proposed uses of land;
(4) To conduct, along with the building official, inspections of premises and preliminary investigations regarding the compliance of buildings, other structures (including fences), and other proposed uses of land with applicable ordinances, codes and regulations;
(5) To recommend to the municipal planning commission or other appropriate agency that applications for permits for the construction of buildings and other structures (including fences) and for other proposed uses of land be granted, denied or conditioned on the applicant's fulfillment of specified requirements or obligations;
(6) To perform such additional tasks and functions, directly related to the foregoing, as may be specifically requested by the chair of the municipal planning commission, the chair of the board of zoning appeals, or the mayor;
(7) To keep and maintain current records relating to all the foregoing.
(b) The building and land use administrator's authority shall be advisory only with all final decisions and determinations within the jurisdiction of the municipal planning commission, board of zoning appeals or city council to be made by those agencies.
(Ord. No. 310, § 2, 7-12-2018)
